An issue occurs in `tests/subsys/fs/fcb/src/main.c` because `fcb_tc_pretest()` does not reset the `struct fcb` instance (specifically `f_scratch_cnt`) before re-initializing it for each test. When a test in `fcb_test_with_4sectors_set` (such as `test_fcb_last_of_n` or `test_fcb_multi_scratch`) sets `test_fcb.f_scratch_cnt = 1U`, that setting persists into subsequent 2-sector tests like `test_fcb_append_fill`, causing one of the two sectors to be reserved as a scratch sector instead of being filled.

Resetting `_fcb` in `fcb_tc_pretest()` (while preserving `f_flags` for `test_fcb_crc_disabled`) resolves the issue.

